# The archive/ tree is retired code kept for history, not the running product.
# Without this, GitHub's Languages panel measured it: 489 of the repository's
# 500 TypeScript files and most of its CSS live in archive/, so the panel
# described a frontend that stopped being shipped. Marking it vendored leaves
# the files exactly where they are and stops them being counted as what we
# build. scripts/verify-language-coverage-floors.mjs excludes the same tree, so
# the panel and the coverage assurance now measure the same thing.
archive/** linguist-vendored
